{#
    Cloudflare Turnstile widget (explicit render via the `turnstile` Stimulus
    controller in assets/controllers/turnstile_controller.js).

    Explicit rendering is mandatory here because Turbo Drive is enabled app-wide
    (assets/controllers.json -> @symfony/ux-turbo/turbo-core). Cloudflare's
    api.js scans for `.cf-turnstile` only once, when the script first executes,
    so a Turbo body swap would leave the widget unrendered. The controller
    renders on connect and calls turnstile.remove() on disconnect, so the widget
    survives navigation in both directions.

    Do NOT also load api.js from a {% block javascripts %}. A second, implicit-mode
    copy of the script suppresses the explicit render and the widget disappears.

    The Spin telemetry marker is passed as `data-turnstile-action-value`, not
    `data-action` -- Stimulus would try to parse the latter as an action descriptor.

    Params:
        size - normal (default) | flexible | compact
#}
<div data-controller="turnstile"
     data-turnstile-sitekey-value="{{ cloudflare_turnstile_site_key }}"
     data-turnstile-action-value="turnstile-spin-v2"
     data-turnstile-size-value="{{ size|default('normal') }}">
    <div class="cf-turnstile" data-turnstile-target="widget"></div>
</div>
